    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0572" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg502"/>

                <head>No. 296.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 8, 1883</date>.
                        (Received June 9.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 19th
                    ultimo, and to previou s correspondence on the subject, I have the honor to
                    inclose to you extract <pb facs="0573" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> of a letter from
                    the Hon. E. Dewdney, lieutenant-governor of the Northwest Provinces, to the
                    secretary of the Governor-General, respecting the incursions of the Piegan
                    Indians.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d296-a1.xml" xpointer="d296-a1"/>
            </div>
